{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,220p' /home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed1583749884/6/codegen_prompts/5.md\"","aggregated_output":"你要为一个新的 ARC-AGI 风格题目实现代码。代码文件必须包含 `main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray` 和 `generate_input() -> np.ndarray`。\n\n## 新题位置\n\n- 描述目录：`/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/6`\n- 题号：`5`\n- 目标代码路径：`/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed1583749884/6/5.py`\n\n## 新题描述\n\n<new_puzzle index=\"5\">\n- `description`：将每个容器内标记像素的排列模式作为\"钥匙\"，与图例中的模式匹配后，用图例指定的颜色重绘容器边框。\n\n- `Input structure`：\n  - 背景为 Black。\n  - 网格上方有一个图例区域，包含 3-4 个由 Grey 分隔的小格子。每个格子内有一个简单的 2x3 或 3x2 的 Yellow 像素排列模式（如对角线、十字、L 形等），格子下方紧贴一个 1x1 的彩色色块（如 Red、Blue、Green）。\n  - 网格下方有若干个由 Maroon 像素构成的一像素厚封闭矩形框（容器），每个容器内部散布着若干 Yellow 像素，排列成某种模式。\n\n- `Rule`：\n  - 对每个容器，提取其内部的 Yellow 像素的归一化排列模式（平移到左上角对齐）。\n  - 在图例中找到匹配该模式的格子，读取其关联的颜色色块。\n  - 将该容器的 Maroon 边框重着色为匹配的颜色。\n  - 保持容器内部的 Yellow 像素和图例不变。\n\n- `Key insight`：容器内部的 Yellow 排列模式是查找键，而非装饰物；图例建立了模式到颜色的映射，两者的匹配关系需要从样例中归纳。\n</new_puzzle>\n\n## 机制相似参考题\n\n下面参考题由本地相似度流程自动选择：先用 `annotations`/docstring/代码特征抽取机制标签，再按机制相似度、文本相似度和代码特征相似度重排，并用 MMR 做去重。优先学习这些题的对象识别方式、随机生成器约束、边界条件处理，不要照搬旧题规则。\n\n已选参考：eval/88e364bc, train/e734a0e8, train/2ccd9fef, eval/a32d8b75, train/2e65ae53, eval/89565ca0, eval/581f7754, eval/65b59efc\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"1\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"88e364bc\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.4112\nmechanism=0.4965\nlexical=0.0253\ncode_feature=0.5714\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:bfs, code:connected_components, code:rotation, object:closed_region, object:frame, object:marker, object:rectangle, object:template, operation:translate, relation:direction, relation:inside, relation:row_col\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/88e364bc.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/88e364bc.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nSlide yellow pixels inside walled regions in the direction dictated by border-legend arrows.\n\nInput structure:\n- bg = most common color; yellow pixels sit inside enclosed regions bounded by colored walls.\n- Border legends: small rectangles on the grid edge whose fill color C matches a region's border color. Each legend contains a center dot and an indicator dot encoding a direction.\n\nRule:\n- For each enclosed region, identify its border color C and look up the legend with fill color C.\n- The direction from the legend's center dot to its indicator dot gives the slide direction.\n- All yellow pixels in that region slide in that direction, stacking against the far wall.\n\nKey insight: Legend fill color links to region border color; the center→indicator offset encodes the movement vector.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"summary\": \"Yellow pixels inside colored-border regions move in the direction indicated by the red pixel in the legend with matching background color, stopping at region boundary.\",\n  \"type\": \"move_along_path\",\n  \"src\": \"yellow pixels inside colored-border regions s\",\n  \"dst\": null,\n  \"match_cond\": \"\",\n  \"path\": \"move(s, direction=legend.red_pixel_offset) where legend.background_color == s.containing_region.border_color until s.touches(region_boundary)\",\n  \"trajectory\": \"\",\n  \"transform\": \"\",\n  \"symbol_instructions\": \"legend on grid edge with background color C and red pixel indicates: yellow pixels in regions with border color C move in direction from blue center to red pixel\",\n  \"multi_step\": \"\",\n  \"concepts\": [\n    \"legend/control-pixels\",\n    \"region-membership\",\n    \"directional-movement\",\n    \"boundary-collision\"\n  ],\n  \"notes\": \"\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"2\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"e734a0e8\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.3422\nmechanism=0.4227\nlexical=0.0171\ncode_feature=0.4286\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:bfs, code:rotation, object:axis, object:marker, object:rectangle, object:template, operation:translate, relation:row_col\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/e734a0e8.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/e734a0e8.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nCopy the unique colored sprite tile into every tiled cell marked by an internal separator-colored pixel.\n\nInput structure\n- Full same-color separator rows and columns partition the grid into equal rectangular tiles.\n- One tile contains the only non-background, non-separator colored sprite.\n- Target tiles are otherwise background-colored but contain at least one internal pixel of the separator color.\n\nRule\n- Keep the separator lines and the source sprite tile unchanged.\n- Replace each marked target tile with an exact copy of the source tile.\n- Unmarked background-only tiles remain unchanged.\n\nKey insight\n- The internal separator-colored pixels are placement markers; the single colored tile is the template to stamp into those marked cells.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"type\": \"move_to_match\",\n  \"src\": \"unique colored sprite tile s in the separator grid\",\n  \"dst\": \"marked background tile d containing an internal separator-colored marker pixel\",\n  \"match_cond\": \"every marked d receives the same unique s\",\n  \"transform\": \"replace d with an exact copy of s, erasing the marker\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"3\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"2ccd9fef\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.3167\nmechanism=0.3854\nlexical=0.0160\ncode_feature=0.4286\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:connected_components, code:rotation, object:axis, object:frame, object:rectangle, object:template, operation:shape_match, relation:row_col\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/2ccd9fef.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/2ccd9fef.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nPredict the next panel in a framed sequence by continuing each scheduled colored interval.\n\nInput structure\n- The grid is made from three or more equal panels in one row or one column.\n- The final input panel is the static target template; every earlier panel differs from it only by dynamic colors absent from the template.\n- Each dynamic color appears in a regular temporal schedule across the earlier panels.\n\nRule\n- Keep the final template panel as the output canvas.\n- For every dynamic color whose schedule reaches the next panel, compare its last two appearances.\n- Extrapolate each one-dimensional interval along the color's changing row or column axis and paint that predicted mask.\n\nKey insight\n- The task is not asking for the last visible panel, but for the next frame after the blank/template slot.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"type\": \"symmetry/pattern\",\n  \"src\": \"sequence of equal rectangular panels ending with a blank/static template panel\",\n  \"dst\": \"next panel in the sequence\",\n  \"transform\": \"use the template panel as the output canvas; for each dynamic color absent from the template, follow its regular panel schedule and extrapolate the last two interval changes one more step along the changing row or column axis\",\n  \"grid_shape\": \"same shape as one panel\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"4\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"a32d8b75\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.3124\nmechanism=0.3544\nlexical=0.0140\ncode_feature=0.5714\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:bfs, code:connected_components, code:rotation, object:axis, object:frame, object:marker, object:template, operation:translate, relation:direction, relation:row_col\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/a32d8b75.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/a32d8b75.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nAssemble and place enlarged sprites on a canvas using legend-panel instructions.\n\nInput structure:\n- Color-6 separators divide the grid into a left legend column and a main canvas.\n- Each legend panel has (top to bottom): a unit sprite, a frame template, a 5x5 bordered square with a position-marker pixel, and a 3x3 rotation clock-hand.\n\nRule:\n- Tile the unit sprite into each active cell of the frame to build an enlarged composite.\n- Rotate the composite per the clock-hand direction (up=0, right=90, down=180, left=270 degrees).\n- Place it on the canvas anchored at the position encoded by the marker pixel's row/col in the bordered square's 3x3 inner grid.\n\nKey insight: The marker pixel's position in a 3x3 grid jointly encodes vertical and horizontal anchor alignment (start/middle/end).\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"summary\": \"Use four legend icons on the left to construct a large sprite by combining unit sprite with frame shape, then place it on background at position and rotation indicated by position marker and rotation marker.\",\n  \"type\": \"move_to_match\",\n  \"src\": \"unit sprite pattern from legend row 1 s1\",\n  \"dst\": \"each foreground pixel position in frame shape from legend row 2 d1\",\n  \"match_cond\": \"s1 replaces each pixel of d1.frame to create enlarged composite sprite\",\n  \"path\": \"\",\n  \"trajectory\": \"\",\n  \"transform\": \"tile s1 at each d1.pixel position to form fractal-like enlarged sprite\",\n  \"symbol_instructions\": \"legend row 1: unit sprite pattern; legend row 2: frame shape template; legend row 3: position marker (pixel location in small square indicates anchor on background); legend row 4: rotation indicator (clock-hand style determines rotation angle)\",\n  \"multi_step\": \"Step 1: read four legend icons from left column; Step 2: construct enlarged sprite by tiling unit sprite into frame shape; Step 3: determine placement position from position marker; Step 4: determine rotation from rotation marker; Step 5: place rotated enlarged sprite at indicated position on background\",\n  \"concepts\": [\n    \"fractal-like tiling\",\n    \"rotation\",\n    \"position encoding\",\n    \"legend interpretation\",\n    \"sprite composition\"\n  ],\n  \"notes\": \"\",\n  \"type2\": \"move_to_match\",\n  \"src2\": \"the constructed enlarged sprite s2\",\n  \"dst2\": \"position on main background grid d2\",\n  \"match_cond2\": \"s2.anchor == position indicated by marker pixel in legend row 3 square; s2.rotation == rotation indicated by clock-hand marker in legend row 4\",\n  \"path2\": \"\",\n  \"trajectory2\": \"\",\n  \"transform2\": \"rotate(s2, angle from legend row 4) then place at d2\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"5\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"2e65ae53\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.3055\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
